// PLAYTEST: does a Medic's repair routine buy back a round, or is it a
// second health bar you pay Power for?
//
// One of seven files — `player-class-striker`, `-bastion`, `-medic`,
// `-saboteur`, `-leech`, `-invoker`, `-decompiler` — identical in every field but `character`. See
// `player-class-striker.ron` for the shared argument: why the pack is this
// pack, why the pool is unspent, and why **the headless bin reports the same
// numbers for all seven at this level** (it plays All-Attack and invokes
// nothing, so it is the floor rather than the measurement). At level 8 and
// above that stops being true — a Striker's second ordinary swing is
// something the bin does see.
//
//     FERAL_DEV_ARENA=1 cargo run  ->  [R] Arena  ->  [L] player-class-medic
//
// The floor, 2026-09-01, 20 reps, seeds 1-20: 60% won, mean 18.6 rounds,
// 26% player Integrity left, 1.15 companions down. Compare deltas within one
// build only.
//
// This is the class the fight is most likely to reward and the one most
// likely to reward it for the wrong reason. Companions rarely drop here
// (1.15 a fight, out of two) and the player is who takes the damage, so a
// Medic in this party is mostly healing *themselves*. If that is the only
// thing the heal is ever for, the class reads as a bigger Integrity pool
// rather than as a role — which is the finding, not a tuning bug.
//
// What to watch:
//   - Patch Single at 1.3 restores a band around 25 authored power. Against
//     a level-5 player that is a meaningful fraction of the bar; is it more
//     than the damage the round cost you?
//   - Medic damps Damage at 0.8. That never touches your swing, only an
//     invoked damage routine — and this kit has none. So the trade is
//     invisible in this fight, deliberately: swap the routine to
//     `stack_smash` on the wizard and fight it again to see the other half.
//   - The turn you choose to heal on. A heal spent early is wasted and a
//     heal spent late is a round you did not have. Whether that decision
//     exists at all is the question this file is really asking.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 5, zone: 1),
    character: (
        class: Some(Medic),
        stats: (0, 0, 0, 0),
        routine: Some("checksum_repair"),
    ),
    party: [
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
        (species: "glitch", level: 5),
    ],
    opponents: [
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
        (species: "sub_process", count: 5),
    ],
    reps: 1,
    seed: 2,
)
